<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kaskaskia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kaskaskia were one of the main peoples of the Illinois Confederation, an Algonquian-speaking alliance of the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a> valley. In 1673 their Grand Village on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/illinois">Illinois</a> river near Starved Rock was visited by Marquette and Jolliet. In 1703 they moved south to the river now named after them, where the French settlement of Kaskaskia grew up, and their descendants belong to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoria">Peoria</a> Tribe of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oklahoma">Oklahoma</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kaskaskia.jpg" alt="Kaskaskia" width="229" height="337" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: General Georges-Henri-Victor Collot · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kaskaskia_Illinois.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
